## Solution

**Setup.** We have the hierarchical model $Z \mid \mu \sim N(\mu,1)$ with $\mu \sim N(0,1)$, so marginally $Z \sim N(0,2)$. Also $X \sim \exp(\lambda)$ (rate $\lambda$, density $\lambda e^{-\lambda x}$, $x\ge 0$), independent of $Z$.

**Key reduction.** Conditioning on $Z$ and using the survival function of the exponential:

$$\mathbb{P}_\lambda(Z^2 \le X) = \mathbb{E}\big[\mathbb{P}(X \ge Z^2 \mid Z)\big] = \mathbb{E}\big[e^{-\lambda Z^2}\big].$$

**Computing the Gaussian integral.** With $Z \sim N(0,2)$, density $\frac{1}{\sqrt{4\pi}}e^{-z^2/4}$:

$$\mathbb{E}[e^{-\lambda Z^2}] = \frac{1}{\sqrt{4\pi}}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-(\lambda+1/4)z^2}\,dz = \frac{1}{\sqrt{4\pi}}\cdot\sqrt{\frac{\pi}{\lambda+1/4}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1+4\lambda}}.$$

**Asymptotics as $\lambda\to 0^+$.** Expanding:

$$\mathbb{P}_\lambda(Z^2 \le X) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{1+4\lambda}} = 1 - 2\lambda + 6\lambda^2 - \cdots$$

so

$$1 - \mathbb{P}_\lambda(Z^2 \le X) = 1 - \frac{1}{\sqrt{1+4\lambda}} \sim 2\lambda \quad (\lambda\to 0^+).$$

**Conclusion.** The probability $\mathbb{P}_\lambda(Z^2\le X) = \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{1+4\lambda}} \to 1$ as $\lambda\to 0^+$, with leading-order correction

$$\boxed{\mathbb{P}_\lambda(Z^2 \le X) = 1 - 2\lambda + O(\lambda^2), \qquad \text{i.e. } 1-\mathbb{P}_\lambda(Z^2\le X)\sim 2\lambda.}$$

### PROOF COMPLETE
